--- !u!114 &734675972
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 734675970}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 30e8e37d88289204784a0442b3c88612, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - 'Connect (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of all used modules to the
    (220 VAC) terminal and the neutral path (N) of the main board. '
  - Connect an Ethernet cable from the Main frame (Comm. Out) to the wind mill module
    (Comm. In)
  - Connect (L1), (L2), and (L3) terminals of the Generator Output from the wind
    mill module to the (L1), (L2), and (L3) input terminals of the Full Bridge Rectifier
    module.
  - Connect the rectifier's (+VE) terminal to terminal (1) of the Rheostat.
  - Connect terminal (3) of the Rheostat to the rectifier's (-VE) terminal.
  - Release the emergency stop button on the main board
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the main board.
  - Switch on the main board ON/OFF switch.
  - Release the emergency button on the wind mill.
  - Raise the circuit breaker (C.B) of the wind turbine.
  - Switch on the wind mill ON/OFF.
  - 'Enable the generator output enable/ disable switch to allow the

    voltage
    to reach the input of the rectifier module'
  - 'Gradually decrease the rheostat''s resistance (increase the load) by turning
    its knob counter-clockwise. '
  - Switch to the software monitor.
  - Navigate to the "Graph" tab.
  - Select the graph of the Speed (RPM) vs. DC voltage.
  - Now, gradually increase the wind mill speed.
  - You have finished! You can now select another experiment.
  popups:
  - afterStep: 11
    text: The speeds of the generator and the motor increase and the voltage increases
      on the power analyzer.
  - afterStep: 12
    text: Observe that the current increases while the voltage drops.
  - afterStep: 17
    text: Observe that the system compensates for the voltage drop by increasing
      the output voltage as speed increases.
  stepItemPrefab: {fileID: 6570533322573217691, guid: cd25d304eaf4809488e7c6b299d13404, type: 3}
  contentParent: {fileID: 734675971}
